-- title:
--   Joint residues of f-integral functions: integrality and monic denominators
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field and $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring, with residue field $k =$ `IsLocalRing.ResidueField A`; let $F$ be a field extension of $L$, let $\iota$ be a finite index type, and for each $i$ let $\bar F_i$ be a field that is a $k$-algebra. For each $i$ let $R_i$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ to $F$ with residue field $\bar F_i$: a valuation subring $\mathcal O_i \subseteq F$ together with a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho_i \colon \mathcal O_i \to \bar F_i$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_i$, such that an element of $L$ lies in $\mathcal O_i$ exactly when it lies in $A$, such that $\rho_i$ agrees on $A$ with $A \to k \to \bar F_i$, and such that every nonzero $f \in F$ has an $L$-multiple lying in $\mathcal O_i$ with nonzero residue. Assume the $\mathcal O_i$ are pairwise distinct, i.e. $i \mapsto \mathcal O_i$ is injective. Let $f \in F$ lie in every $\mathcal O_i$, assume $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $L(f)$ generated by $f$, assume each residue $\bar f_i = \rho_i(f)$ is transcendental over $k$, and assume $\sum_i [\bar F_i : k(\bar f_i)] = [F : L(f)]$, the degrees being taken over the intermediate fields generated by $\bar f_i$ and by $f$ respectively. Let $S \subseteq \prod_i \bar F_i$ consist of the vectors $(\rho_i(u))_i$ for those $u \in F$ that lie in every $\mathcal O_i$ and moreover lie in every valuation subring $V$ of $F$ containing the image of $L$ and containing $f$, and let $\rho(T)$ be the $k$-submodule of $\prod_i \bar F_i$ spanned by $S$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions. First, for every $h \in \rho(T)$, every $i$, and every place $w$ of $\bar F_i$ over $k$ — that is, a valuation subring of $\bar F_i$ containing the image of $k$, different from $\bar F_i$, and a principal ideal ring — one has $\operatorname{ord}_w(h_i) \ge 0$ whenever $\operatorname{ord}_w(\bar f_i) \ge 0$, where $\operatorname{ord}_w$ is the integer-valued order attached to $w$ via its associated adic valuation. Second, for every $h \in \prod_i \bar F_i$ there is a monic polynomial $c \in k[X]$ such that $(c(\bar f_i) \, h_i)_i$ lies in $\rho(T)$.
--
--   This is the Deuring-style reduction step for function fields: it says that the joint residues of the functions regular where $f$ is regular have no poles outside the poles of $\bar f_i$, and that after clearing a monic denominator in $\bar f$ every vector of residues is attained, so that the family $(R_i)$ captures all of $\prod_i \bar F_i$ up to $k[\bar f]$-denominators. It is stated here under the additional assumption that $L$ is algebraically closed, which is what its consumers need, and it feeds the dimension estimates [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_forall_finrank_residueSpan_inf_add_card_le`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_forall_finrank_residueSpan_inf_add_card_le) and [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_forall_finrank_residueSpan_inf_add_card_le_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_forall_finrank_residueSpan_inf_add_card_le_of_isAlgClosed).
